+config DSA_HOST_MEMORY
+	bool "DSA: show apps the memory the guest may grow to as the device's"
+	depends on PROC_FS
+	default n
+	help
+	  The Desktop Subsystem for Android guest starts small and grows, so
+	  its memory size says nothing about what an app may use. This shows
+	  every app process (Android app ID 10000 or more) the memory the
+	  guest may grow to (kernel.dsa_host_memory.total_kb in bootconfig)
+	  as MemTotal in /proc/meminfo and as totalram in sysinfo(), and adds
+	  what the guest may still grow to its free and available memory.
+	  The app store named in /sys/module/dsa_host_memory/parameters/uids
+	  sees the computer's memory (store_total_kb) as its total. System
+	  processes, and the apps named in real_uids, see the guest's own
+	  memory.
+
+	  Unless you are building the DSA guest kernel, say N.
+
